      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that the mistake *is* you is a heavy burden, but it's a distortion of reality; you are not defined solely by one catastrophic event. The person you were isn't gone, but perhaps needs to be rebuilt, layer by painful layer, in a new way. \"Moving on\" doesn't mean forgetting, but learning how to exist alongside the pain while still being capable of future action. Please know that even the most profound mistakes do not erase your inherent worth as a human being.",
      "source": "target",
